Third-party material
--------------------
The mascot bitmaps in ios/GadgetKit/Sources/GadgetKit/Pixel/MascotFrames.swift and
android/core/src/main/kotlin/com/tozes/hermescompanion/core/MascotFrames.kt
(generated by scripts/generate-assets.py), the app icon ios/AppIcon.png (drawn by
scripts/make-icon.py) and the Android launcher icon layers in
android/app/src/main/res/mipmap-*/ic_launcher_foreground.png and
ic_launcher_monochrome.png (drawn by scripts/make-android-icon.py) all come
from the Hermes Gadget SDK's
firmware/core/src/mascot_data.cpp, which is itself generated from
assets/mascot/nous-girl-white-1024.png. That artwork comes from the Hermes Agent
repository, https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent, released under the
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research. The mascot is Nous Research's
character and part of their brand; check with Nous Research before using it
outside Hermes-related projects.

The 5x7 pixel font in ios/Sources/HermesCompanion/Pixel/PixelFontGlyphs.swift and
android/core/src/main/kotlin/com/tozes/hermescompanion/core/PixelFontGlyphs.kt
is ported from the Hermes Gadget SDK's firmware/core/src/font5x7.cpp,
https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-gadget-sdk, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026
Hermes Gadget SDK contributors.

The colours follow the SDK's firmware renderer (firmware/core/src/ui.cpp) and
project site (site/src/styles.css), from the same repository
and license.
